# Docker Runtime Validation

Manual acceptance testing runs in Docker containers. **Compilation happens on the host**
(local Maven / pnpm), then artifacts are copied into runtime images — no Maven/npm inside
`docker build`.

## Non-negotiables

1. **Deploy entry (queued)** — `.\scripts\docker-deploy-queue.ps1` (mutex around
   `docker-deploy.ps1`). Bare `docker-deploy.ps1` only when debugging with the lock held.
2. **Test URLs** — UI `http://localhost:4173`, health `http://localhost:8080/healthz`.
3. **After behavior changes** — queued redeploy before claiming acceptance Done.

## Gate commands

| Context | Command |
| --- | --- |
| Backend TDD | `mvn -B -ntp -f backend/pom.xml -Pdev-fast test` |
| Backend full gate | `mvn -B -ntp -f backend/pom.xml verify` |
| Frontend full gates | `pnpm -C frontend lint && type-check && test && build` |
| Deploy queued | `.\scripts\docker-deploy-queue.ps1` |
| E2E docker | `pnpm -C frontend test:e2e:docker` |

## Forbidden

- Parallel acceptance stacks / second `COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME` / ad-hoc port offsets.
- Claiming Done without redeploy after behavior changes.
- `mvn verify` for TDD inner loops — use `-Pdev-fast test`.

